{"data":{"id":"10.1594/pangaea.958394","type":"dois","attributes":{"doi":"10.1594/pangaea.958394","prefix":"10.1594","suffix":"pangaea.958394","identifiers":[],"alternateIdentifiers":[],"titles":[{"title":"Continuous thermosalinograph oceanography along RV METEOR cruise track M181"}],"publisher":"PANGAEA","container":{},"publicationYear":2023,"subjects":[{"subject":"DATE/TIME","subjectScheme":"Parameter"},{"subject":"LATITUDE","subjectScheme":"Parameter"},{"subject":"LONGITUDE","subjectScheme":"Parameter"},{"subject":"DEPTH, water","subjectScheme":"Parameter"},{"subject":"Temperature, water","subjectScheme":"Parameter"},{"subject":"Quality flag, water temperature","subjectScheme":"Parameter"},{"subject":"Conductivity","subjectScheme":"Parameter"},{"subject":"Temperature, water, internal","subjectScheme":"Parameter"},{"subject":"Salinity","subjectScheme":"Parameter"},{"subject":"Quality flag, salinity","subjectScheme":"Parameter"},{"subject":"Measurement container","subjectScheme":"Parameter"},{"subject":"Thermosalinograph","subjectScheme":"Method"},{"subject":"Digital oceanographic thermometer, Sea-Bird, SBE 38","subjectScheme":"Method"},{"subject":"Seadatanet flag: Data quality control procedures according to SeaDataNet (2010)","subjectScheme":"Method"},{"subject":"Thermosalinograph (TSG), Sea-Bird, SBE 21 SEACAT","subjectScheme":"Method"},{"subject":"Calculated from internal temperature and conductivity","subjectScheme":"Method"},{"subject":"Salinometer","subjectScheme":"Method"},{"subject":"M181","subjectScheme":"Campaign"},{"subject":"Meteor (1986)","subjectScheme":"Basis"},{"subject":"DAM Underway Research Data (DAM_Underway)","subjectScheme":"Project"},{"subject":"DataHub Earth and Environment of the Helmholtz Association (DataHub)","subjectScheme":"Project"}],"dates":[{"date":"2022-04-21T12:51:00/2022-05-27T10:26:00","dateType":"Collected"}],"language":"en","types":{"ris":"DATA","bibtex":"misc","citeproc":"dataset","schemaOrg":"Dataset","resourceType":"Dataset","resourceTypeGeneral":"Dataset"},"relatedIdentifiers":[{"relationType":"IsObsoletedBy","relatedIdentifier":"10.1594/pangaea.997226","relatedIdentifierType":"DOI"},{"relationType":"IsDocumentedBy","relatedIdentifier":"10.5281/zenodo.7535545","relatedIdentifierType":"DOI"}],"relatedItems":[],"sizes":["338397 data points"],"formats":["text/tab-separated-values"],"version":null,"rightsList":[{"rights":"Licensing unknown: Please contact principal investigator/authors to gain access and request licensing terms","rightsIdentifier":"unknown","rightsIdentifierScheme":"SPDX"},{"rights":"Data access is restricted (moratorium, sensitive data, license constraints)"}],"descriptions":[{"description":"Underway temperature and salinity data was collected along the cruise track with two autonomous thermosalinograph (TSG) systems, each consisting of a SBE21 TSG together with a SBE38 Thermometer. Both systems worked independent from each other throughout the cruise. While temperature is taken at the water inlet in about 5 m depth, salinity is estimated within the interior TSG from conductivity and interior temperature. Temperature and salinity were calibrated against CTD data from 5 m depth. For details to all processing steps see Data Processing Report.","descriptionType":"Abstract"},{"description":"Temperature was calibrated independently for both TSGs against CTD data from 5 m depth. Value added to temperature data TSG1 = -0.004999. Value added to temperature data TSG2 = -0.002784.Salinity was calibrated independently for both TSGs against CTD data from 5 m depth (tim is the time in days since Expocode of this cruise (06M320220417), i.e. since 2022-04-17T00:00:00): Value added to salinity data TSG1 = 0.0008591*tim-0.01788. Value added to salinity data TSG2 = 0.0004812*tim++0.02843. TSG1 was chosen for publication.","descriptionType":"TechnicalInfo"}],"geoLocations":[{"geoLocationBox":{"eastBoundLongitude":18.3559486,"northBoundLatitude":17.1780666,"southBoundLatitude":-33.8495508